{title: Simple Gifts}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse}
'Tis the [G]gift to be simple, 'tis the [C]gift to be [G]free,
'Tis the [G]gift to come down where we [D]ought to [D7]be,
And [G]when we find ourselves in the [C]place just [G]right,
'Twill be [G]in the valley of [D]love and de[G]light.

{c: Chorus}
When [C]true simplicity is [G]gained,
To [C]bow and to bend we shan't be a[G]shamed,
To [G]turn, turn will be our de[D]light,
Till by [G]turning, turning we [D]come round [G]right.
